# The scenes of the fake-behind-an-interface deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# fake-behind-an-interface.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in fake-behind-an-interface.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the interface
note "The shop talks to its message queue through an *interface*. Messages are delivered on commit."
show MessageQueue 3 13 "the shop's interface to the queue" --zoom 9-12

## Scene 2: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's order placement. Look at where it *commits*."
show TodaysOrderPlacement 16 22 "today's order placement" --zoom 18-20

## Scene 3: the mock test
note "A test with a *mock* queue: it checks each call was made."
show MockedQueueTest 16 23 "the mock test" --zoom 20-22

## Scene 4: the fake
note "A *fake* queue: it holds messages until commit, then delivers them, like the real queue."
show InMemoryMessageQueue 10 29 "the fake queue" --zoom 21-23

## Scene 5: the fake test
note "A test with the *fake*: it checks what was *delivered*."
show FakeQueueTest 13 20 "the fake test" --zoom 18-19

## Scene 6: the fake finds the bug
note "Run the tests against today's order placement:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:fake-behind-an-interface:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The mock test passes. The fake shows the fraud check never arrives: it was sent after the commit."

## Scene 7: the fixed order placement
note "The order placement that commits once, at the end:"
show FixedOrderPlacement 16 22 "the fixed order placement" --zoom 21
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:fake-behind-an-interface:test"
callout "Both messages are delivered. The fake checks results, so it doesn't care how the code gets there."
